---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import VerifyOffline from '../../components/VerifyOffline.astro';
---

<Base
  title="AudioLocal | Privacy"
  description="AudioLocal's privacy policy. Your audio, video and PDF files are converted in your browser and are not uploaded to any server."
  path="/en/privacy.html"
  alternate="/privacy.html"
  lang="en"
  active="privacy"
  ogTitle="AudioLocal — Privacy"
  ogDescription="How AudioLocal handles your files and your personal data."
  ogImageAlt="Privacy at AudioLocal, local conversion in your browser"
>
  <article class="doc prose">
    <h1 class="title">Your files, your privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Today, every AudioLocal tool runs in your browser. No file leaves your device.</p>
    <p class="updated-note">No file uploads · No sign-up or account · No tracking cookies · <a href="https://github.com/Andrespb404/AudioLocal" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Public code on GitHub</a></p>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>100% local processing</h2>
      <p>AudioLocal converts your audio, video and PDF files directly in your browser, using JavaScript and the browser's media features. Your files never leave your device, are not uploaded to any server, and are cleared automatically from the page when you close the tab or reload it. Whatever you download stays on your device.</p>
    </section>

    <VerifyOffline lang="en" class="doc-section" />

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Information we do NOT collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your files or their contents</li>
        <li>Sign-up data: there are no accounts</li>
        <li>Conversion history</li>
        <li>User profiles or cross-site tracking</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Visit statistics</h2>
      <p>We use <strong>Vercel Web Analytics</strong> to learn how many people visit the site and how they get here. For each page view it records the page and its filtered parameters, the site you came from (for example, Google), the date, your approximate location, and your type of device, operating system and browser.</p>
      <p>It doesn't use cookies. To count visitors it uses an identifier created from the request, which is discarded after 24 hours, and we only see aggregated statistics. It never includes your files or their names. See <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how Vercel handles this data</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Technical hosting data</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on <strong>Vercel</strong>, which logs technical data for each visit (such as the IP address, the date and the page requested) to serve and protect the site. Your files don't travel in those requests. See its <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <p>With some PDFs, the browser asks the site for helper files, such as fonts or character maps. That request never includes your document or its name.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>We use <strong>localStorage</strong> only to save your conversion preferences (output format, channels, sample rate, etc.). These preferences stay in your browser, and you can delete them at any time.</p>
      <p>To work offline, a <strong>service worker</strong> saves the site's files (pages, styles, scripts and fonts) in your browser's cache. It never saves your files, and you can clear it from your browser settings.</p>
      <p>We don't use tracking cookies or third-party advertising.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Donations (Ko-fi)</h2>
      <p>This site accepts voluntary donations through <strong>Ko-fi</strong>. Clicking the donation link takes you to ko-fi.com, which has its own privacy policy. If you donate, we receive your display name and email; the payment is handled by Ko-fi and its processor, and we don't see your card details.</p>
      <p>You can read Ko-fi's policy at: <a href="https://ko-fi.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ko-fi.com/privacy</a></p>
      <p>If you email us, we receive your address and whatever you send.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>This policy applies only to AudioLocal. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of other websites you may reach through links.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Site owner</h2>
      <p>AudioLocal is an independent project.<br />Contact email: <a href="mailto:audiolocal.app@gmail.com">audiolocal.app@gmail.com</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The current version will always be the one published on this page. The date of the last update appears at the end.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="updated-note">Last updated: November 7, 2026</p>
  </article>
</Base>
